# Jenkins Installation and Configuration on AWS EC2 (Amazon Linux 2)#

## 🧩 Overview
This documentation explains the step-by-step process of installing and configuring **Jenkins** on an **AWS EC2** instance using **Amazon Linux 2**.  
Jenkins is an open-source automation server widely used for **Continuous Integration (CI)** and **Continuous Deployment (CD)**.

---

## ☁️ 1. Launch EC2 Instance

### EC2 Configuration:
- **AMI:** Amazon Linux 2 (Free Tier)
- **Instance Type:** t2.medium
- **Key Pair:** Create or use existing `.pem` file
- **Storage:** Default (8 GB or more)
- **Security Group Inbound Rules:**

| Type | Protocol | Port | Source | Purpose |
|------|-----------|------|---------|----------|
| SSH | TCP | 22 | My IP | Connect via terminal |
| HTTP | TCP | 80 | Anywhere | Web access |
| Custom TCP | TCP | 8080 | Anywhere | Jenkins web interface |

> Port 8080 is required for accessing Jenkins through your browser.

